## 5️⃣  Common pitfalls & how to avoid them

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **No tiles appear, network tab shows 404 for `cache://…`** | The protocol was registered *after* the map was created. | Call `maplibregl.addProtocol` **before** `new maplibregl.Map(...)`. |
| **Tiles are always fetched from the network, even though they are cached** | Handler rejected (or threw) before returning the cached data. | Verify that `getTile` returns an `ArrayBuffer` and that you **resolve** with `{ data: blob }`. |
| **AbortController errors** | The handler ignored `abortCtrl.signal`. | Check `abortCtrl.signal.aborted` early and return a rejected promise if true. |
| **`URL` parsing fails for `cache://…`** | Using `new URL('cache://…')` in older browsers that don’t support custom schemes. | All modern browsers (Chrome ≥ 71, Edge ≥ 79, Firefox ≥ 60, Safari ≥ 12) support it. If you need to support older browsers, split the string manually (`url.split('://')[1]`). |
| **Large tiles cause UI jank** | The IndexedDB read is done on the main thread. | `idb-keyval` already uses the browser’s async IndexedDB API, which runs off the UI thread. No extra work needed. |
| **Cache-first + network fallback not working** | The handler resolves with `null` instead of rejecting. | **Reject** (`throw new Error('not cached')`) when the tile is missing; MapLibre will then try the `fallback` URLs or its default HTTP stack. |

